{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question","id":406978,"title":"Quick Coil of Zirnitra Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-15T14:31:59-08:00","id":406978,"title":"Quick Coil of Zirnitra Question","content":"Referencing this.<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">The Coil of Zirnitra</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">This ancient Coil is named after a Slavic dragon god of sorcery. Zirnitra\u2019s Coil is nearly extinct; to most Order sensibilities, it offers limited rewards and great risk. Functionally, it removes an oft-overlooked weakness of the Kindred condition: the penchant for developing mortal magics and psychic phenomena. Some Dragons have developed this Coil to regain the lost gifts granted to them by their heritage as part of a werewolf family. Some use it to recover the magics tied to their mortal bloodlines. Merits must still be purchased; this Coil allows that purchase.</span></span></span><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_J83T-t9g-87pvtUTKCZIJ2QQzCTOzUclkWJjsvb814/edit#heading=h.3yrs39jq6n1s\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_J83T-t9g-87pvtUTKCZIJ2QQzCTOzUclkWJjsvb814/edit#heading=h.3yrs39jq6n1s\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_J83T-t9g-87pvtUTKCZIJ2QQzCTOzUclkWJjsvb814/edit#heading=h.3yrs39jq6n1s\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_J83T-t9g-87pvtUTKCZIJ2QQzCTOzUclkWJjsvb814/edit#heading=h.3yrs39jq6n1s </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The text implies that the most common use of the Coil of Zirnitra is to recover lost powers. That makes perfect sense. However, if the Vampire is bitten with the &quot;interested in psychics/whatever&quot; bug, can they use this coil to develop new powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T16:08:27-08:00","id":407100,"title":"","content":"Yes, vampires can do that, provided there's some explanation for how they could gain the power. That could be something that would work for a mortal, or it might be something resembling a Scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T17:01:16-08:00","id":407143,"title":"","content":"I'd actually like to append something to SoulGambit's question. This has been bugging me for a while. Could vampires learn to manifest pyrokinesis, or photokinesis of the sunlight variety? It seems... Quite unthematic that vampires could learn to manifest their own banes from their own power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T19:23:02-08:00","id":407259,"title":"","content":"@Rose: Thanks for the swift reply! <br /> <br /> Actually processing learning supernatural merits in a process similar to Scales is pretty interesting. Can make for nice stories too. Try and capture people with that ability to study them and understand their power, then copy it. Like Sylar meets Cold War Mad Science, but hopefully with better writing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T20:21:26-08:00","id":407326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlitzKitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=407143#post407143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd actually like to append something to SoulGambit's question. This has been bugging me for a while. Could vampires learn to manifest pyrokinesis, or photokinesis of the sunlight variety? It seems... Quite unthematic that vampires could learn to manifest their own banes from their own power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't do that at my table, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T20:32:23-08:00","id":407335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=407326#post407326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't do that at my table, no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, probably. I'd use rumours of it as a dramatic device. But, frankly, Kindred society would come down hard on that if word got out. It's basically a plot time bomb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T03:16:01-08:00","id":407544,"title":"","content":"Also, as even sorcery has manipulating and creating those banes banned (fire, sunlight), it would be a bit odd for pyrokinesis to be a thing vampires could get. It seems fire is so inimical to them those powers are imposible to develope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T03:39:32-08:00","id":407565,"title":"","content":"There would also be a bit of a logical problem with a character even managing to get more than one dot. Considering how little control the Dragon has over their powers at the first dot, the likelihood of them not ashing themselves (either through the Drawback or Failure-turned-Dramatic) before even developing the second dot are quite slim and even then it would still be highly dangerous until they reach the fourth dot. Even by Order standards anyone trying would be suicidal.<br /> <br /> That is not even talking about how the Dragon's own powers would regularly trigger frenzy, unless they are also an avid Ascendant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T04:12:23-08:00","id":407574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=407565#post407565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There would also be a bit of a logical problem with a character even managing to get more than one dot. Considering how little control the Dragon has over their powers at the first dot, the likelihood of them not ashing themselves (either through the Drawback or Failure-turned-Dramatic) before even developing the second dot are quite slim and even then it would still be highly dangerous until they reach the fourth dot. Even by Order standards anyone trying would be suicidal.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an object lesson if there ever was one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T10:37:31-08:00","id":407940,"title":"","content":"Does Clear Eyes count as a Supernatural merit? Because it does specify mortal-only, and one WP one Vitae to become immune to Nightmare and Obfuscate for a scene is pretty damn neat (up there with City Walking in terms of &quot;I have interesting PC ideas using it.&quot;)<br /> <br /> Also, I <i>really</i> hope you aren't still going with the Scale that lets you steal powers from other splats; I mean, it's cool and all, but it also isn't a very good idea, in terms of &quot;it makes the Coil of Zirnitra too damn tempting&quot;. I'd like to see a Scale that lets you take the &quot;Ghoul&quot; merits, where your Sire counts as your Regnant and which lets you extract blood from other Kindred to qualify for the other ones.<br /> <br /> I'm talking about the Taste of &lt;Blank&gt; merits here, not stuff like Watch Dog. Think of it as a minor &quot;refinement&quot; of your Clan.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T13:01:54-08:00","id":410459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=407326#post407326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't do that at my table, no.</div> </div> </div> </div> Dang it! I mean, it's not something to get before 5 Dots in, but I actually kind-of liked the idea of &quot;The Voivode of Flame&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T14:02:10-08:00","id":410523,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth I've done it at mine. Albeit the character in question is an ancient Jiang Shi with close to a dozen other bizarre powers, and is thoroughly an NPC. But it does the trick to drive home just how far off she is from the 'base state' of vampirism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T17:06:59-08:00","id":415888,"title":"","content":"<b>What kind of creature powers can the scale nab? Like a Changeling's ability to open hedge gates? Or a kith ability? Or a contract? I'm still not 100% sure on this side of it.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T17:58:28-08:00","id":415935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=407940#post407940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Clear Eyes count as a Supernatural merit? Because it does specify mortal-only, and one WP one Vitae to become immune to Nightmare and Obfuscate for a scene is pretty damn neat (up there with City Walking in terms of &quot;I have interesting PC ideas using it.&quot;)<br /> <br /> Also, I <i>really</i> hope you aren't still going with the Scale that lets you steal powers from other splats; I mean, it's cool and all, but it also isn't a very good idea, in terms of &quot;it makes the Coil of Zirnitra too damn tempting&quot;. I'd like to see a Scale that lets you take the &quot;Ghoul&quot; merits, where your Sire counts as your Regnant and which lets you extract blood from other Kindred to qualify for the other ones.<br /> <br /> I'm talking about the Taste of &lt;Blank&gt; merits here, not stuff like Watch Dog. Think of it as a minor &quot;refinement&quot; of your Clan.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that it's not that simple to just take the body part/power away from another supernatural. For one, they tend to have societies that frown at their members being dissected and/or killed. For another, you need to know what they are and what they're capable of ahead of time, and then need a way to capture them without them in any of that time realizing you're a threat (or again, society). And it's likely a Humanity breaking point if the individual is in any way human. So it's hardly 'too tempting', you need to be a very specific sort of.... dedicated, to be able to make good use of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T18:28:02-08:00","id":415957,"title":"","content":"Looking over the different psychic powers, I think Auspex replaces or is better than almost all of them, except the combat ones. And the combat ones are pretty underwhelming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T19:09:26-08:00","id":415973,"title":"","content":"I just realised that if you wanted to make the scale truly horrifying, you could house rule it so that they had to keep the creature alive.....<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T20:20:05-08:00","id":416047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=415935#post415935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Remember that it's not that simple to just take the body part/power away from another supernatural. For one, they tend to have societies that frown at their members being dissected and/or killed. For another, you need to know what they are and what they're capable of ahead of time, and then need a way to capture them without them in any of that time realizing you're a threat (or again, society). And it's likely a Humanity breaking point if the individual is in any way human. So it's hardly 'too tempting', you need to be a very specific sort of.... dedicated, to be able to make good use of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a terrible justification. Just saying.<br /> <br /> You know of a Kindred who has some kind of interesting Bloodline Power? Like, say, a Khaibit?<br /> <br /> Buy an eye from them; they can grow it back <i>trivially</i> next time they go through Daysleep (especially if you give them the Vitae to do so), you can shove it in your head, and boom, you've got Udjat.<br /> <br /> Heck, there are probably <i>tons</i> of Ordo initiates that would trade a hand (Vigor), some skin (Resilience), an eye (Dominate or Auspex), or a tongue (Majesty) in exchange for some Herd access and some training in the Coils.<br /> <br /> Along those lines, set up a meat market with other members of the Ordo; trade a face from a master of the Coil of the Ascendant (to grab The Warm Face) for a hand from some initiate (Vigor); give yourself the face (to grab 24 hour Blush of Life), graft some Vigor dots onto the master, and give the initiate some training or a leg up; just wash everything down with some Vitae and call it good.<br /> <br /> It's a shortcut; it's not even a particularly <i>difficult</i> shortcut, once you notice that the other guy doesn't need to be dead at the end of it, and that you have a society full of Supernaturals walking around <i>with the ability to trivially regrow limbs</i>. I mean, sure, you're going to have a rocky start, getting Kindred to sell or trade body parts. But once they figure out that, hey, there's a <i>pretty good</i> trade going on there, with minimal risk to themselves...<br /> <br /> I mean, imagine someone came up to you on the street and offered you $1000 dollars for a lock of your hair. With no catch.<br /> <br /> Similar arguments can be made for other Supernaturals (like Werewolves) that can trivially regrow body parts; I mean, offer some of your social clout (or whatever other resources you can muster) to a Werewolf's pack in exchange for whatever non-vital organ you've decided is the root of a Werewolf's regeneration. Or their shapeshifting. Or one of their more &quot;physical&quot; Gifts.<br /> <br /> Or let it be known (<i>discretely</i>) that you're in the market for well-preserved Werewolf parts. Lord only knows its not the first time an Ordo member's done <i>that</i>.<br /> <hr /><br /> As for Supernatural Merits being weaker than Auspex... yes and no.<br /> <br /> Yes, Auspex covers most of thenon-combat Supernatural merits... Except for stuff like <b>Omen Sensitivity</b> (which is far broader than any of Auspex's dots), <b>Unseen Senses</b> (Strix) (I'm pretty sure Auspex can't auto-find Strix), <b>City Walking</b> (Auspex doesn't let you teleport between cities! Granted, I don't think <i>any</i> Discipline does), <b>Clear Sighted</b> (again, one Willpower and one Vitae to be <i>immune to two Disciplines for a Scene</i>), or <b>Medium</b> (Ghosts aren't something normal Kindred powers deal with. And Ghosts are <i>useful</i>).<br /> <br /> Of the combat ones, the standouts are <b>Numbing Touch</b> (damage Willpower as part of an Unarmed Attack? Which gives a <i>pretty big penalty</i> to all dice pools for a few turns? Pretty. Darn. Good), <b>Telekinesis</b> (redirect <i>all</i> ranged attacks for a turn by spending one Vitae and one Willpower? Increase &quot;Strength&quot; for 1xp instead of 4xp?), and <b>Psychokinesis</b> (barring cheesy ones like fire or sunlight, stuff like Psychokinesis (Blood) or Psychokinesis (Electricity) are pretty useful.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T23:28:04-08:00","id":416215,"title":"","content":"The person you take an organ from can't grow it back while you benefit from it. <br /> <br /> Doesn't Auspex 1 let you identify Strix? I'm pretty sure using it is like spending willpower on a perception roll. Omen Sensitivity, City Walking, and Medium are all good points. Numbing Touch I'll give you only because you can use it as part of an unarmed attack. I'm not actually sure how to read that power. As far as I can see, it's Spend 1 WP to touch someone and numb them with the roll. Spend 2 WP to use it as part of an unarmed attack, drain WP, and bypass the need for a roll at all?<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how you get that Telekinesis redirects range attacks. Though I wonder if you can use it to disarm or steal. The attack version is pretty meh because it's penalized by Stamina, which is affected by Physical Intensity (and resilience).<br /> <br /> Psychokinesis... can be good for utility I guess. Blood, Wood, Metal, Shadow and Electricity being the real winners there. I would probably *not* allow blood created/manifested by I'd totally like some ideas for creative uses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T23:41:03-08:00","id":416221,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I missed that bit. Still, Vampires are nothing if not good at social stuff, so...<br /> <br /> One of the options for Grappling lets you redirect ranged attacks to the person you're grappling. Telekinesis lets you grapple people from a range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T23:41:28-08:00","id":416222,"title":"","content":"Well for blood, I'd say you can totally create it... but it will lack the nourishment required to a vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T00:53:27-08:00","id":416264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=416222#post416222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well for blood, I'd say you can totally create it... but it will lack the nourishment required to a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course; Vitae isn't <i>blood</i>, after all.<br /> <br /> Now, Psychokinesis (Vitae) <i>is</i> technically a viable choice, but that would get you smacked. Hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T01:26:01-08:00","id":416287,"title":"","content":"/smacks amechra just for the suggestion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T03:15:10-08:00","id":416327,"title":"","content":"Thinking of some interesting psychokinesis uses...<br /> <br /> <b>Metal</b><br /> - Shrink / Warp weapons to the point of unsuitability.<br /> - Make guns point and fire, magneto style.<br /> - Large scale structural damage.<br /> - Building / fortification <br /> <br /> <b>Blood</b><br /> - Moving and storing blood.<br /> - Ripping blood out of wounds for feeding (Not sure if possible???)<br /> - One of the more subtle ways to kill someone (spontaneous heart attack)<br /> <br /> <b>Wood/Plants</b><br /> - Psychic Staking.<br /> - Large scale structure building/destroying/shaping.<br /> - Grow or destroy plants.<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow</b><br /> - Increase size to create stuff to hide in / obscure vision.<br /> <br /> <b>Electricity</b><br /> - Power or turn off electronic devices.<br /> <br /> <br /> Xylokinesis is particularly useful. The rote, physical intensity'd action can stake most people. If Fire is off the table it's probably the best pure Psychic Combat option.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T03:44:26-08:00","id":416345,"title":"","content":"Bloodbending, the cheaper alternative to Dominate's level 5 Possession and doesn't require you to leave your own body. You just look like a mime while you use it. Alternatively you can temporarily hinder or cut off a vampire's access to their disciplines.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T03:54:44-08:00","id":416346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=416047#post416047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a terrible justification. Just saying.<br /> <br /> You know of a Kindred who has some kind of interesting Bloodline Power? Like, say, a Khaibit?<br /> <br /> Buy an eye from them; they can grow it back <i>trivially</i> next time they go through Daysleep (especially if you give them the Vitae to do so), you can shove it in your head, and boom, you've got Udjat.<br /> <br /> Heck, there are probably <i>tons</i> of Ordo initiates that would trade a hand (Vigor), some skin (Resilience), an eye (Dominate or Auspex), or a tongue (Majesty) in exchange for some Herd access and some training in the Coils.<br /> <br /> Along those lines, set up a meat market with other members of the Ordo; trade a face from a master of the Coil of the Ascendant (to grab The Warm Face) for a hand from some initiate (Vigor); give yourself the face (to grab 24 hour Blush of Life), graft some Vigor dots onto the master, and give the initiate some training or a leg up; just wash everything down with some Vitae and call it good.<br /> <br /> It's a shortcut; it's not even a particularly <i>difficult</i> shortcut, once you notice that the other guy doesn't need to be dead at the end of it, and that you have a society full of Supernaturals walking around <i>with the ability to trivially regrow limbs</i>. I mean, sure, you're going to have a rocky start, getting Kindred to sell or trade body parts. But once they figure out that, hey, there's a <i>pretty good</i> trade going on there, with minimal risk to themselves...<br /> <br /> I mean, imagine someone came up to you on the street and offered you $1000 dollars for a lock of your hair. With no catch.<br /> <br /> Similar arguments can be made for other Supernaturals (like Werewolves) that can trivially regrow body parts; I mean, offer some of your social clout (or whatever other resources you can muster) to a Werewolf's pack in exchange for whatever non-vital organ you've decided is the root of a Werewolf's regeneration. Or their shapeshifting. Or one of their more &quot;physical&quot; Gifts.<br /> <br /> Or let it be known (<i>discretely</i>) that you're in the market for well-preserved Werewolf parts. Lord only knows its not the first time an Ordo member's done <i>that</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you not read the power?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">If the victim survives the surgery, she loses access to the ability so long as the body part remains detached. She similarly loses any ability to regenerate that part.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The body part CANNOT be grown back, and the power taken cannot be used by the character. NOBODY will ever let you take a part of them voluntarily, unless theyre permanently done with both that power and that body part for some reason, so that nullifies your argument there. There's no shortcut; you're taking the power from someone, permanently, and crippling them somehow, permanently. You similarly can't just take an old body part you find lying around; you need to detach it for the purpose of the scale at a Wyrm's Nest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T04:43:40-08:00","id":416381,"title":"","content":"No need to get snippy; again, that does shift it from &quot;Surgical Trades&quot; to &quot;Ordo's Corpse Disposal.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, Dominate and Majesty really widen the boundaries of &quot;voluntary.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Oh, and <i>Producer</i>. You know that Merit that could make infinite Vitae loops if a Ghoul had it (hence it being changed to Human only)? Graft it from a Human with the ability onto a Ghoul. Infinite Vitae LOOP!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 02-23-2015, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T04:52:56-08:00","id":416389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=416381#post416381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No need to get snippy; again, that does shift it from &quot;Surgical Trades&quot; to &quot;Ordo's Corpse Disposal.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, Dominate and Majesty really widen the boundaries of &quot;voluntary.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't trying to be snippy, sorry.<br /> <br /> Regardless, defaulting to Dominate and Majesty can still bring up the main point I made. When ~Steve~ the mage goes back home missing an eye and tells his cabalmates that &quot;The most charming pale individual asked for my eye, and since then I haven't been able to see the Supernal through the lens of Death, but I just couldn't say no to that face&quot;, you get other mages looking into it and then bad things can happen to the Vampire.<br /> <br /> (And yes, I know, you can be more careful with how you word the Dominate/Majesty usage, but bottom line is one way or another it causes other mages/changelings/whatever to look into it once the missing body part or the missing individual is noticed)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T05:02:23-08:00","id":416399,"title":"","content":"Mages seem like one of the &quot;bad idea&quot; cases.<br /> <br /> But, hey, bill yourself as a corpse disposal specialist; if a Mage kills another Mage, hey, you'll dispose of that little body for them, no questions asked. Offer to sit in with Mages doing dissections on whatever weird beastie they've killed in exchange for some body parts for your own research.<br /> <br /> Heck, there'd probably be Mages <i>fascinated</i> by the whole &quot;gaining new powers through grafts&quot; thing. Probably not enough to go through with being a &quot;donor&quot; themselves, but they might slip you bodyparts in exchange for studying <i>you</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T05:08:36-08:00","id":416403,"title":"","content":"As soon as this Coil was previewed I wove in a story about a vampire who had learned it, and had grafted on some Mage-parts.<br /> <br /> Vampires don't have Awakened souls, and thus can not contain Paradox.<br /> <br /> That was great fun, and a cautionary tale to the players for when they get hold of that mystery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T05:09:41-08:00","id":416404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=416399#post416399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages seem like one of the &quot;bad idea&quot; cases.<br /> <br /> But, hey, bill yourself as a corpse disposal specialist; if a Mage kills another Mage, hey, you'll dispose of that little body for them, no questions asked. Offer to sit in with Mages doing dissections on whatever weird beastie they've killed in exchange for some body parts for your own research.<br /> <br /> Heck, there'd probably be Mages <i>fascinated</i> by the whole &quot;gaining new powers through grafts&quot; thing. Probably not enough to go through with being a &quot;donor&quot; themselves, but they might slip you bodyparts in exchange for studying <i>you</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might work, if they happen to do dissections on a Hallow (or other wyrm's nest) that they don't mind a Vampire being at. You'd also need to know what powers the person/beastie had, and the body part that suits that power needs to be accessible and not decomposed yet.<br /> <br /> But sure, yes, that might work for a given individual, if they can set it up. And that's one of those specialized cases that probably won't be doable for every member of the Ordo, meaning it's still not something everyone's going to be too tempted to take. You need to build a concept around it or else you basically get killed while doing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T05:57:40-08:00","id":416428,"title":"","content":"More psychokinesis ideas:<br /> <br /> \u2022Ice: Seems thematic enough for a living corpse to use. Also, an excuse to sing Let It Go whenever you want!<br /> \u2022Water: It's everywhere! And people cam drown in even a tiny amount of water...<br /> \u2022Light(NOT sunlight): I admit, it's not as thematic as the others, but if having my Vampire shoot (non-Bane) Laser Beams is wrong, I don't want to be right!<br /> \u2022Glass: Not as common as water, but close enough in any urban environment.<br /> \u2022Air: Killing someone by draining the air from their lungs does not leave that much evidence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T06:11:43-08:00","id":416435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=416403#post416403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As soon as this Coil was previewed I wove in a story about a vampire who had learned it, and had grafted on some Mage-parts.<br /> <br /> Vampires don't have Awakened souls, and thus can not contain Paradox.<br /> <br /> That was great fun, and a cautionary tale to the players for when they get hold of that mystery.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sleepers don't have awakened souls either, by definition, but you do know that they handle paradox, like say from invoking an enchanted item, the same as mages, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T06:32:18-08:00","id":416442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=416435#post416435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sleepers don't have awakened souls either, by definition, but you do know that they handle paradox, like say from invoking an enchanted item, the same as mages, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but then it was the Mage who created the item who is behind it.<br /> <br /> I mostly based this on Brookshaw's mention in the DevBlog that when a Mage in 2e gets his soul stolen, he can't contain Paradoxes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T10:47:30-08:00","id":416647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=416399#post416399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages seem like one of the &quot;bad idea&quot; cases.<br /> <br /> But, hey, bill yourself as a corpse disposal specialist; if a Mage kills another Mage, hey, you'll dispose of that little body for them, no questions asked. Offer to sit in with Mages doing dissections on whatever weird beastie they've killed in exchange for some body parts for your own research.<br /> <br /> Heck, there'd probably be Mages <i>fascinated</i> by the whole &quot;gaining new powers through grafts&quot; thing. Probably not enough to go through with being a &quot;donor&quot; themselves, but they might slip you bodyparts in exchange for studying <i>you</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The supernatural has to be alive when the vampire removes the limb, organ, or tissue to be grafted. Hence the line about &quot;If it survives, thi this and this happen&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T12:56:49-08:00","id":416777,"title":"","content":"I hate to rain on the parade, but the psychokinesis merit is described as the manipulation of a force. The examples include manifestations of force so I guess those are okay too, not much practical difference really. Known forces include electricity, magnetism, gravity, nuclear, and friction. Common manifestations of forces would be heat, cold, light, radiation, sound, wind, weather, and earthquakes. Wind for air, magnetism for metal, cold for ice (cold + water = ice), heat for fire (heat + combustibles = fire) would all make sense. A weaker argument could be made to include fire and ice as they are also manifestations of force. It just so happens the merit includes fire so go crazy. Fire is not however matter. Things like metal, blood and wood are out. A force might manipulate one of those things, but you would not create them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T14:12:55-08:00","id":416876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=416647#post416647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The supernatural has to be alive when the vampire removes the limb, organ, or tissue to be grafted. Hence the line about &quot;If it survives, thi this and this happen&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, it never actually mentions that they have to be alive.<br /> <br /> That line is just for if you decide to get your extractin' on when the critter's still alive.<br /> <br /> The only <i>real</i> requirement is that it hasn't decayed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T14:44:33-08:00","id":416900,"title":"","content":"Consider that most supernaturals revert to, essentially, human upon death.<br /> <br /> Once the mind and soul have vacated the body, a mage corpse is no different than a human corpse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T15:21:31-08:00","id":416926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=416876#post416876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, it never actually mentions that they have to be alive.<br /> <br /> That line is just for if you decide to get your extractin' on when the critter's still alive.<br /> <br /> The only <i>real</i> requirement is that it hasn't decayed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think everyone could agree that blatantly saying they need to be alive would help balance or clarify the power, then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T16:02:51-08:00","id":416947,"title":"","content":"I would agree that <i>not having the Scale to begin with</i> would help, but yes.<br /> <br /> Seriously, though, it feels... out of place? Alright, hear me out on this one:<br /> <br /> The Coil is about reclaiming former powers <i>of the mind</i>, fluffwise. The other scale is about shielding people from mind control by lobotomizing them (which is cool and thematic.) Grafting body parts from other creatures just feels like an attempt to shoe-horn Vicissitude in; I'd much prefer to see Scales dealing with twisted psychological experiments, or &quot;experimental&quot; brain surgeries. Grafts should be specific and... messy, with stuff like opening up &quot;third eyes&quot; or engorging the pituary gland so that you can speak to Eris.<br /> <br /> As it is, the Scale is either too niche, or too strong to pass up on if you're going Ordo. I mean, it's missing any information on how you would deal with traits you don't have (like Rank or Renown) and it's <i>incredibly</i> vague on what you can steal.<br /> <br /> Can I steal a Werewolf's ability to shapeshift if I come up with the right bullshit? Can I take a Demon's ability to form covers, lie perfectly, or spoof? What about a Sin-Eater's ability to reincarnate? Ooh, how about a Mummy's ability to Seal Flesh? Why not a Changeling's Mask?<br /> <br /> Or, in a <i>completely facetious</i> line of enquiry, could I steal that Changeling's ability to spend Glamour? How about a Vampire's ability to Frenzy, Lash Out, or Embrace; a Promethean's ability to infect others with Disquiet? Maybe that Demon's ability to Go Loud?<br /> <br /> Even by the strictest interpretation I can think of (you can only buy <i>abilities that you actually have to activate</i>), you still get into the area of mechanical widgets interacting in ways they were never supposed to. I know that there's a Demon Form power that renders you entirely immune to Fire, for one thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T17:13:57-08:00","id":416987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=416947#post416947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would agree that <i>not having the Scale to begin with</i> would help, but yes.<br /> <br /> Seriously, though, it feels... out of place? Alright, hear me out on this one:<br /> <br /> The Coil is about reclaiming former powers <i>of the mind</i>, fluffwise. The other scale is about shielding people from mind control by lobotomizing them (which is cool and thematic.) Grafting body parts from other creatures just feels like an attempt to shoe-horn Vicissitude in; I'd much prefer to see Scales dealing with twisted psychological experiments, or &quot;experimental&quot; brain surgeries. Grafts should be specific and... messy, with stuff like opening up &quot;third eyes&quot; or engorging the pituary gland so that you can speak to Eris.<br /> <br /> As it is, the Scale is either too niche, or too strong to pass up on if you're going Ordo. I mean, it's missing any information on how you would deal with traits you don't have (like Rank or Renown) and it's <i>incredibly</i> vague on what you can steal.<br /> <br /> Can I steal a Werewolf's ability to shapeshift if I come up with the right bullshit? Can I take a Demon's ability to form covers, lie perfectly, or spoof? What about a Sin-Eater's ability to reincarnate? Ooh, how about a Mummy's ability to Seal Flesh? Why not a Changeling's Mask?<br /> <br /> Or, in a <i>completely facetious</i> line of enquiry, could I steal that Changeling's ability to spend Glamour? How about a Vampire's ability to Frenzy, Lash Out, or Embrace; a Promethean's ability to infect others with Disquiet? Maybe that Demon's ability to Go Loud?<br /> <br /> Even by the strictest interpretation I can think of (you can only buy <i>abilities that you actually have to activate</i>), you still get into the area of mechanical widgets interacting in ways they were never supposed to. I know that there's a Demon Form power that renders you entirely immune to Fire, for one thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of that sounds more like it needs more detail than it shouldn't exist, which I'd also agree with. Definitely could use some clarifications and a bit more detail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","e