rs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T14:38:18-08:00","id":417981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=417402#post417402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually going to agree mostly with Diggs, but with less science and less Nuclearkinesis. Blood, Metal, and Wood, etc are probably not valid psychokinesis targets, although I'm pretty sure &quot;ice&quot; is for cyrokinesis. So maybe cold is considered a &quot;force&quot; in this context? Magnetism for metal is still probably fine.<br /> <br /> You know what else the Coil probably allows? Some hunter merits, particularly Benediction and Castigation. While it may not allow the direct purchase of Chiron Group's stuff... I feel like practitioners of the Coil of Zimitra would be making very much the same things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... I don't think it does; Endowments are unique to <i>Hunters</i>, not <i>Mortals</i>. Also, Benediction or Castigation would be pretty borked; you get up to five powers in exchange for one of your Supernatural Merit picks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T14:41:52-08:00","id":418001,"title":"","content":"I would imagine that a Vampire who was Lucefuge before embrace could get some of his Castigations back, if he lost them on embrace, since it specifically mentions powers tied to bloodlines.<br /> <br /> And the number of merits restriction goes away as your dots in the coil go up.<br /> <br /> At least one writer has said that, at their table, Benediction and Theban Sorcery were different ways of invoking the same magic, so I doubt this coil could give you benediction anymore than it could give you Theban Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T17:25:47-08:00","id":418122,"title":"","content":"Endowments aren't supernatural merits, IMHO, they're a Hunter-only merit of their own type, I'd call them. So you'd probably need to use a Scale and cut out the endowments with a knife if you wanted them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T18:31:02-08:00","id":418175,"title":"","content":"Except Castigation, which inborn magical power(Supernatural) that is derived from the Lucifuge bloodline. And Endowments are merits.<br /> <br /> Supernatural Powers derived from bloodline is explicitly a thing vampires can get with this coil, and Castigation is a merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T18:52:39-08:00","id":418190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=418175#post418175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except Castigation, which inborn magical power(Supernatural) that is derived from the Lucifuge bloodline. And Endowments are merits.<br /> <br /> Supernatural Powers derived from bloodline is explicitly a thing vampires can get with this coil, and Castigation is a merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Castigation was an inborn ability, a member of Lucifage wouldn't be able to unlearn/forget those spell abilities and trade them out for different spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T19:48:30-08:00","id":418262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=418190#post418190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If Castigation was an inborn ability, a member of Lucifuge wouldn't be able to unlearn/forget those spell abilities and trade them out for different spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not actually mutually exclusive-the potential to learn those spells in an inborn supernatural ability. The spells themselves are learned applications of that ability.<br /> <br /> If it <i>wasn't </i>inborn, then anyone could learn castigation-not just the Lucifuge and others of their bloodline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T20:27:11-08:00","id":418286,"title":"","content":"Actually, no, endowments aren't hunter specific, they're conspiracy specific, or else Slashers couldn't retain their endowments.<br /> <br /> Also, spirit slayers gives reasons as to why werewolves can or cannot have specific endowments, if endowments were hunter specific the rule would be &quot;werewolves can't have endowments, not here's why they can't have this specific endowment.&quot; You don't list specific reasons when there's a catchall ban. <br /> <br /> And as I've already mentioned, Cheiron gives out thaumatech enhancements to witch and vampire informants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T20:30:44-08:00","id":418290,"title":"","content":"(I'm thinking I should bow out of this one; I'm worked up about it enough that I'm making simple errors with regards to research and reading. So Amechra out! I hope you cats enjoy the rest of the thread.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T04:45:04-08:00","id":418596,"title":"","content":"The Coil does call out Supernatural Merits specifically, which is a category of merit. A merit NEEDS to be listed under that type to be something you can take, and the Rules Update for Hunter in Mortal remains doesn't say anything about giving Endowments that categorization. So, while an ST COULD say that they do count, by RAW you could not use this coil to take Endowments, strictly speaking. It doesn't matter if they're supernatural powers that happen to be merits; they need to be in the category the Coil allows for specifically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T04:52:51-08:00","id":418597,"title":"","content":"...Endowments, no matter what kind, are considered<i> Endowment</i> merits. Some may also be considered to have supernatural effects, but without special circumstances &amp; good justification, Zirnitra does not let you pick them up. In cases such as Advanced Armory &amp; Relics, the power is external &amp; not relevant to this discussion. Castigation might be possible but no switching out abilities or learning ones you didn't know in life, etc.<br /> <br /> As always it depends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T05:02:44-08:00","id":418601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=418597#post418597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Endowments, no matter what kind, are considered<i> Endowment</i> merits. Some may also be considered to have supernatural effects, but without special circumstances &amp; good justification, Zirnitra does not let you pick them up. In cases such as Advanced Armory &amp; Relics, the power is external &amp; not relevant to this discussion. Castigation might be possible but no switching out abilities or learning ones you didn't know in life, etc.<br /> <br /> As always it depends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, the coil says nothing about being <i>exclusively</i> for regaining powers you had in life. The first tier says that it is often used for that, but the coil's true purpose is to regain the use of psychic powers and hedge magics that mortals can wield by the kindred can't.<br /> <br /> Thus, a kindred belonging to the Lucifuge bloodline in life should, theoretically, be able to develop castigation as a power with this coil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T05:14:50-08:00","id":418605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=418601#post418601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, the coil says nothing about being <i>exclusively</i> for regaining powers you had in life. The first tier says that it is often used for that, but the coil's true purpose is to regain the use of psychic powers and hedge magics that mortals can wield by the kindred can't.<br /> <br /> Thus, a kindred belonging to the Lucifuge bloodline in life should, theoretically, be able to develop castigation as a power with this coil.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> but not by RAW <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T05:45:33-08:00","id":418630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=418601#post418601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, the coil says nothing about being <i>exclusively</i> for regaining powers you had in life. The first tier says that it is often used for that, but the coil's true purpose is to regain the use of psychic powers and hedge magics that mortals can wield by the kindred can't.<br /> <br /> Thus, a kindred belonging to the Lucifuge bloodline in life should, theoretically, be able to develop castigation as a power with this coil.</div> </div> </div> </div>It DOES say it's specifically for SUPERNATURAL merits, though, as in that specific category, not just merits that have a supernatural feel to them, so by RAW endowments don't count, and thus can't be taken, by the rules given in the Coil's writeup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T06:49:13-08:00","id":418658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=418630#post418630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It DOES say it's specifically for SUPERNATURAL merits, though, as in that specific category, not just merits that have a supernatural feel to them, so by RAW endowments don't count, and thus can't be taken, by the rules given in the Coil's writeup.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it specifically say &quot;Supernatural merits, as the category&quot;? Because that's an entirely different thing from &quot;Supernatural merits&quot; and even if it does, nowhere in the hunter book does it say that entitlements are a fifth category of merit.<br /> <br /> Vampires have vampire only merits, but those are still split between the &quot;social, mental, physical, supernatural&quot; categories.<br /> <br /> Why would hunter merits not also be the same? Especially since hunter merits are not hunter exclusive-slashers have them, and Cheiron gives out Thaumatech to non-hunter agents and informants.<br /> <br /> And again by Raw, a vampire can use the coil to regain merits representing powers derived from their supernatural bloodline. Castigation is a merit that represents powers derived from a supernatural bloodline.<br /> <br /> Thus, if the Storyteller lets a player get away with having a character who was in the lucifuge bloodline pre-embrace, and lets that player take this coil, then there's no reason not to let them take castigation as one of their supernatural merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T06:52:48-08:00","id":418663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=418658#post418658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thus, if the Storyteller lets a player get away with having a character who was in the lucifuge bloodline pre-embrace, and lets that player take this coil, then there's no reason not to let them take castigation as one of their supernatural merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the storyteller let's a player get away with it, the character can have fire powers, be invincible, be able to mind control anyone with a reflexive unresistible action, etc etc. <br /> <br /> We're not saying that the ST shouldn't allow this. Simply, that the RAW is not such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T06:59:47-08:00","id":418669,"title":"","content":"So, I decided to put on my quasi-munchkin hat and do some theorycrafting. I do have a newfound respect for the Coil of Zimitra. Opening up Supernatural Merits to Kindred allows for a different set of advantages that have just enough of a niche to be useful without overwhelming actual Kindred powers. The cost break sets them to being just cheap enough to be useful, and allows for easy access to a &quot;reasonable&quot; amount of competence in a large number areas. Essentially, a vampire specializing in the Coil of Zimitra is looking to be a jack of all trades.<br /> <br /> Auspex is better then the supernatural options available at investigating specific questions, people, or places. Supernatural merits are better when you have very little information to go on, or need a broad overview. Clairvoyance and Omen Sensitivity are arguably worth the coil all by themselves.<br /> <br /> In terms of combat, if Psychokinesis remains Lethal against Kindred then it offers a viable if extremely costly alternative to the normal Kindred options. It's a crass &quot;throw a bucket of dice at the problem&quot; option, but it is a decent one. Telekinesis is terrible in Kindred vs Kindred conflict because Physical Intensity trumps it.<br /> <br /> Having poked and proded these builds a bit, I noticed that Kindred on Kindred conflict is <b>costly</b> in terms of blood, with both sides trying to end the conflict as quickly as possible using one-shot kills and ambushes. Notably this means that while any of the following builds are terrifying one on one, a group of opponents can bring most of them down. Even one on one, going through a fight is likely to leave you vulnerable to the next one if you aren't careful. Feeding from your opponent helps with this, but that brings its own trials.<br /> <br /> Another observation is that the key to kindred physical conflict is high blood potency. Note that all of these builds are overly twinked as I'm only counting traits that move towards the test goal. Realistically only about 50-75% of a dedicated character's traits are likely to be dedicated so singularly to combat at the actual table, meaning these builds are more delayed than they first appear.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Gangral</u></b><br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Intelligence 1, Wits 3, Resolve 3, Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3, Presence 2, Manipulation 1, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl 5 [Grappling], Stealth 2 [Ambushing], Weaponry 2, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Swarm Form 3, Acute Senses 1, Indomitable, Trained Observer 3, Defensive Combat [Brawl] 1,<br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Protean 3<br /> <b><i>10 EXP:</i></b> Blood Potency 2, Celerity 1<br /> <b><i>20 EXP:</i></b> Blood Potency 3, Protean 4-5<br /> <b><i>30 EXP:</i></b> Blood Potency 4, Professional Training 5<br /> <b><i>40 EXP:</i></b> Close Quarters Combat 4, Resilience 1-2<br /> <b><i>50 EXP:</i></b> Resilience 3-5<br /> <br /> <i>Highlights</i> Nearly unkillable. Either you catch this vampire by surprise and kill / render unable to defend themselves in one hit (vs Resilience 5) or the best you can hope for is a tie. Lots of fire or lateral thinking are your only other alternatives. Don't discount Swarm Form, even at later EXP values.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Nosferatu</u></b><br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Intelligence 1, Wits 3, Resolve 3, Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3, Presence 2, Manipulation 1, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl 2, Stealth 2 [Ambushing], Weaponry 5 [Improvised], Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Improvised Weapons 3, Light Weapons 2, Professional Training 3, Defensive Combat [Weaponry] 1<br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Obfuscate 2, Celerity 1<br /> <b><i>10 EXP:</i></b> Obfuscate 3, Professional Training 4-5, Blood Potency 2<br /> <b><i>20 EXP:</i></b> Vigor 1-3<br /> <b><i>30 EXP:</i></b> Vigor 4-5, Blood Potency 3<br /> <b><i>40 EXP:</i></b> Blood Potency 4-5<br /> <b><i>50 EXP:</i></b> Trained Observer 3, Indomitable, Acute Senses, Close Quarters Combat 4<br /> <br /> <i>Highlights:</i> Has a nice stealth add-on. If there's anything wood near this person, they can improvise it into a weapon and then have a very good chance of staking an opponent. Dicepool of 24 (29 during a Frenzy) with Rote and 9-Again before defense on an improvised stake that deal 8L base damage means most things are pretty screwed. You generally want to get the drop on people if at all possible. The primary defense tactic is to Celerity then Obfuscate away until the situation is more in the character's favor.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Zimitra Vampire</u></b><br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 2, Resolve 4, Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2, Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Occult 5 [Psychokinesis], Empathy 4, Streetwise 3<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Status [Ordo Dracule] 1, Safe Place 1, Nest Guardian 1, Crucible 3, Psychokinesis 5*<br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Coil of Zimitra 1*, Celerity 1, ??? 1<br /> <b><i>10 EXP:</i></b> Coil of Zimitra 2-5*, Area of Expertise [Psychokinesis] 1, Professional Training 2<br /> <b><i>20 EXP:</i></b> Blood Potency 2-3<br /> <b><i>30 EXP:</i></b> Blood Potency 4-5<br /> <b><i>40 EXP:</i></b> Professional Training 3-5, Acute Senses 1, Indomitable, Trained Observer 3, Clear-Sighted 2*<br /> <b><i>50 EXP:</i></b> Telepathy 3*, City Walker 3*, Clairvoyance 3*, Omen Sensitivity 3*, Danger Sense 2<br /> *: Note Discounted EXP cost<br /> <br /> <i>Highlights:</i> You're looking at an utterly obscene 26 (Rote, 9-Again) dice pool for Psychokinesis (before factoring in Resolve) when going all out. That's enough to destroy almost anything. This costs a lot less EXP to &quot;top out&quot; and has easier access to utility. I *think* Psychokinesis still deals lethal damage to Vampires. This guy is an absolutely *terrifying* Sheriff thanks to Clairvoyance, Omen Sensitivity, Telepathy and City Walker.<br /> <br /> I am not sure Zimitra actually allows for Clear-Sighted. If not it's easily replaced with something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 02-25-2015, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T07:16:31-08:00","id":418682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=418669#post418669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I decided to put on my quasi-munchkin hat and do some theorycrafting. I do have a newfound respect for the Coil of Zimitra. Opening up Supernatural Merits to Kindred allows for a different set of advantages that have just enough of a niche to be useful without overwhelming actual Kindred powers. The cost break sets them to being just cheap enough to be useful, and allows for easy access to a &quot;reasonable&quot; amount of competence in a large number areas. Essentially, a vampire specializing in the Coil of Zimitra is looking to be a jack of all trades.<br /> <br /> Auspex is better then the supernatural options available at investigating specific questions, people, or places. Supernatural merits are better when you have very little information to go on, or need a broad overview. Clairvoyance and Omen Sensitivity are arguably worth the coil all by themselves.<br /> <br /> In terms of combat, if Psychokinesis remains Lethal against Kindred then it offers a viable if extremely costly alternative to the normal Kindred options. It's a crass &quot;throw a bucket of dice at the problem&quot; option, but it is a decent one. Telekinesis is terrible in Kindred vs Kindred conflict because Physical Intensity trumps it.<br /> <br /> Having poked and proded these builds a bit, I noticed that Kindred on Kindred conflict is <b>costly</b> in terms of blood, with both sides trying to end the conflict as quickly as possible using one-shot kills and ambushes. Notably this means that while any of the following builds are terrifying one on one, a group of opponents can bring most of them down. Even one on one, going through a fight is likely to leave you vulnerable to the next one if you aren't careful. Feeding from your opponent helps with this, but that brings its own trials.<br /> <br /> Another observation is that the key to kindred physical conflict is high blood potency. Note that all of these builds are overly twinked as I'm only counting traits that move towards the test goal. Realistically only about 50-75% of a dedicated character's traits are likely to be dedicated so singularly to combat at the actual table, meaning these builds are more delayed than they first appear.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Gangral</u></b><br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Intelligence 1, Wits 3, Resolve 3, Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3, Presence 2, Manipulation 1, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl 5 [Grappling], Stealth 2 [Ambushing], Weaponry 2, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Swarm Form 3, Acute Senses 1, Indomitable, Trained Observer 3, Defensive Combat [Brawl] 1,<br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Protean 3<br /> <b><i>10 EXP:</i></b> Blood Potency 2, Celerity 1<br /> <b><i>20 EXP:</i></b> Blood Potency 3, Protean 4-5<br /> <b><i>30 EXP:</i></b> Blood Potency 4, Professional Training 5<br /> <b><i>40 EXP:</i></b> Close Quarters Combat 4, Resilience 1-2<br /> <b><i>50 EXP:</i></b> Resilience 3-5<br /> <br /> <i>Highlights</i> Nearly unkillable. Either you catch this vampire by surprise and kill / render unable to defend themselves in one hit (vs Resilience 5) or the best you can hope for is a tie. Lots of fire or lateral thinking are your only other alternatives. Don't discount Swarm Form, even at later EXP values.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Nosferatu</u></b><br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Intelligence 1, Wits 3, Resolve 3, Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3, Presence 2, Manipulation 1, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl 2, Stealth 2 [Ambushing], Weaponry 5 [Improvised], Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Improvised Weapons 3, Light Weapons 2, Professional Training 3, Defensive Combat [Weaponry] 1<br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Obfuscate 2, Celerity 1<br /> <b><i>10 EXP:</i></b> Obfuscate 3, Professional Training 4-5, Blood Potency 2<br /> <b><i>20 EXP:</i></b> Vigor 1-3<br /> <b><i>30 EXP:</i></b> Vigor 4-5, Blood Potency 3<br /> <b><i>40 EXP:</i></b> Blood Potency 4-5<br /> <b><i>50 EXP:</i></b> Trained Observer 3, Indomitable, Acute Senses, Close Quarters Combat 4<br /> <br /> <i>Highlights:</i> Has a nice stealth add-on. If there's anything wood near this person, they can improvise it into a weapon and then have a very good chance of staking an opponent. Dicepool of 24 (29 during a Frenzy) with Rote and 9-Again before defense on an improvised stake that deal 8L base damage means most things are pretty screwed. You generally want to get the drop on people if at all possible. The primary defense tactic is to Celerity then Obfuscate away until the situation is more in the character's favor.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Zimitra Vampire</u></b><br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 2, Resolve 4, Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2, Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Occult 5 [Psychokinesis], Empathy 4, Streetwise 3<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Status [Ordo Dracule] 1, Safe Place 1, Nest Guardian 1, Crucible 3, Psychokinesis 5*<br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Coil of Zimitra 1*, Celerity 1, ??? 1<br /> <b><i>10 EXP:</i></b> Coil of Zimitra 2-5*, Area of Expertise [Psychokinesis] 1, Professional Training 2<br /> <b><i>20 EXP:</i></b> Blood Potency 2-3<br /> <b><i>30 EXP:</i></b> Blood Potency 4-5<br /> <b><i>40 EXP:</i></b> Professional Training 3-5, Acute Senses 1, Indomitable, Trained Observer 3, Clear-Sighted 2*<br /> <b><i>50 EXP:</i></b> Telepathy 3*, City Walker 3*, Clairvoyance 3*, Omen Sensitivity 3*, Danger Sense 2<br /> *: Note Discounted EXP cost<br /> <br /> <i>Highlights:</i> You're looking at an utterly obscene 26 (Rote, 9-Again) dice pool for Psychokinesis (before factoring in Resolve) when going all out. That's enough to destroy almost anything. This costs a lot less EXP to &quot;top out&quot; and has easier access to utility. I *think* Psychokinesis still deals lethal damage to Vampires. This guy is an absolutely *terrifying* Sheriff thanks to Clairvoyance, Omen Sensitivity, Telepathy and City Walker.<br /> <br /> I am not sure Zimitra actually allows for Clear-Sighted. If not it's easily replaced with something else.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Merits (Professional training) don't work on Disciplines, and I wouldn't allow one to use it on Psychokinesis either (Rote and 9 again). Also, I'm not sure if all out is an option with Psychokinesis","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T07:18:50-08:00","id":418691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=418605#post418605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> but not by RAW <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> By RAW there's no rule that an embraced lucifuge would lose their castigation in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T10:12:51-08:00","id":418895,"title":"","content":"4 (Resolve) + 5 (Skill) +2 (Specialty) +5 (Willpower and Zimitra 4) +10 (Physical Intensity x5) = 26. All Out Attack would make it 29, if allowed. Take 1 Agg damage via Zimitra 5 to make the action Rote. Professional Training just adds 9-Again and gives an alternative way to get Rote for when you don't want to take Agg damage. If you don't want to allow that for some reason or another then that's just 5 more EXP to spend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T10:24:24-08:00","id":418910,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry... physical intensity? On a roll containing Resolve? Or is it something which Zimitra allows? And using Physical Intesnity seriously breaks the strength of this. Any character can be made to look strong with that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T10:39:03-08:00","id":418931,"title":"","content":"Coil of Zirnitra allows you to apply Physical Intensity to rolls to activate Supernatural merits. And also allows you to break the one-Willpower-per-turn limit, but only when spending Willpower on Supernatural merits.<br /> <br /> So a master of the Coil with BP 5 could be looking at +13 dice on a given activation roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T11:07:32-08:00","id":418985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=418658#post418658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it specifically say &quot;Supernatural merits, as the category&quot;? Because that's an entirely different thing from &quot;Supernatural merits&quot; and even if it does, nowhere in the hunter book does it say that entitlements are a fifth category of merit.<br /> <br /> Vampires have vampire only merits, but those are still split between the &quot;social, mental, physical, supernatural&quot; categories.<br /> <br /> Why would hunter merits not also be the same? Especially since hunter merits are not hunter exclusive-slashers have them, and Cheiron gives out Thaumatech to non-hunter agents and informants.<br /> <br /> And again by Raw, a vampire can use the coil to regain merits representing powers derived from their supernatural bloodline. Castigation is a merit that represents powers derived from a supernatural bloodline.<br /> <br /> Thus, if the Storyteller lets a player get away with having a character who was in the lucifuge bloodline pre-embrace, and lets that player take this coil, then there's no reason not to let them take castigation as one of their supernatural merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a longer response ready for this, but it comes down to basically this; that's not how the power works, by RAW. An ST could allow it, but it'd be a house rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T12:47:14-08:00","id":419200,"title":"","content":"So I read about this Coil. Is it really possible now for a Dragon to gain other supernatural creature's powers/abilities? Like steal an organ or a limb and attach it to themselves to gain a werewolf's ability to shapeshift, a mage's magic, or a changeling's contracts. If so...damn...the Dragons are gonna be scary ass dudes. If they can use a werewolf's ability to shapeshift into Gauru, then it will be tough as hell to kill it or defeat it. Hey, that gives me an idea! If this is all possible now then I could make a Dead Wolf to learn this Coil and gain the ability to shapeshift into the other four forms, except urhan (wolf form. Protean 3 for that). Plus it will be able to use Gifts too, not bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T13:07:45-08:00","id":419235,"title":"","content":"Going by this discussion...<br /> <br /> ... it seems to be really... seriously... unclear what the Scale is really supposed to do. I would say, should it actually end up in the book, it needs some more word count to clear that up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T16:02:54-08:00","id":419492,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind the scale is in open development. That means Zimitra and all related material are under review for playtesting. Reaming the devs out about their horribly broken and unbalanced test material that isn't in the final release is a wonderful way to get them to not give more beta material. This goes doubly so since the way you get <i>cool</i> powers is usually, but not always to start high and then slowly chip away until the balance is correct. So, it's all a part of the process. Stay calm and carry on. If you have actual playdata about how this scale, in an actual game, helped or ruined the experience then I'd bet good money that the devs would love you and eat your post up.<br /> <br /> So tl;dr. Scale is a playtest thing and there is a non-zero chance that it will change between what was posted months ago and the final release. I wouldn't get your panties in a bunch over it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T16:47:59-08:00","id":419543,"title":"","content":"Exactly.<br /> <br /> From what I gathered from this discussion is, what we need clear info on is:<br /> <br /> 1) What counts as a Supernatural Merit for this and what does not? Can you take Supernatural Merits normally limited to Minor &amp; Major Templates?<br /> 2) Can you take innate template powers (shape-shifting, mage sight, having Covers, etc)?<br /> 3) Can you take purchasable powers (Gifts, Arcana, Transmutations, etc)?<br /> 4) How far can you stretch the requirement about the body part needing to be symbolic of the power (e.g. no body part seems to be especially emblematic of a Mage's Arcana, except perhaps the brain for Mind)?<br /> 5) Are there any general exceptions to the answers' to the above?<br /> <br /> Alternatively, simply make it clear that what the Coil and Scale can and cannot do is left to the Storyteller's discretion and individual cases should first be discussed with the ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","user":"saibot","date":". 02-25-2015, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T20:54:33-08:00","id":419782,"title":"","content":"It is all in open development. The final version of the coil has not been published so there is no RAW yet. Speculation is fine, but let's not argue about rules that have yet to be written. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> How the coil works with endowments is up in the air. It will probably stay that way. I will say that many endowments are supernatural. You can invalidate a merit for many reasons, but not because it wasn't listed under a supernatural category. It should be obvious what is and is not supernatural. Castigation is supernatural. It may not be a true merit. Maybe the coil doesn't, or shouldn't, allow for re-acquisition of Castigation. I'm not real sure about that, but if it is not allowed then the reason is not that Castigation doesn't qualify as supernatural. That is all I know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T00:41:49-08:00","id":419947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=419782#post419782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is all in open development. The final version of the coil has not been published so there is no RAW yet. Speculation is fine, but let's not argue about rules that have yet to be written. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> How the coil works with endowments is up in the air. It will probably stay that way. I will say that many endowments are supernatural. You can invalidate a merit for many reasons, but not because it wasn't listed under a supernatural category. It should be obvious what is and is not supernatural. Castigation is supernatural. It may not be a true merit. Maybe the coil doesn't, or shouldn't, allow for re-acquisition of Castigation. I'm not real sure about that, but if it is not allowed then the reason is not that Castigation doesn't qualify as supernatural. That is all I know.</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW in this case means what the beta material says and what existing material says. There is a RAW because RAW means rules as written, and we are looking at beta rules as they're written. There's just no final product yet for actual printed RAW.<br /> <br /> As for your own argument, Castigation may be 'supernatural' as in the general adjective, yes, but there is also a specific category of merit called Supernatural Merits, which Castigation is not part of; it's a Hunter merit. It's supernatural, sure, and it's a merit, but it's not in the specific category of Supernatural Merit, which is a deliberately chosen quality of a merit by the writers now, not something an individual ST has to gauge.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the rest, and what others have said, I do agree about not criticizing the Coil too hard, it clearly does need a new draft with some more word count to make it clear what you can and can't get with it. I do think both the Coil and Scale are good additions, though, and hope they remain in the final product.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T06:00:39-08:00","id":420079,"title":"","content":"Show me the place in Hunter Core that says anything about Entitlements being their own category of merit, and most books don't split physical, social, mental, and supernatural merits up in lists.<br /> <br /> Besides, Vampire only, or Werewolf Only, or Mage only merits still follow the &quot;Physical, social, mental, supernatural) split, and Entitlements are not Hunter Specific, as non hunters can have them.<br /> <br /> Besides, RAW also says vampires can use it to regain lost powers from their mortal bloodline, which Castigation does qualify for.<br /> <br /> Even if you're right about merits, Castigation still Qualifies. And if you're wrong, The RAW is self contradictory and should be ignored in that instance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 02-26-2015, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T06:15:49-08:00","id":420086,"title":"","content":"As Saibot said, blessed be his mind, the thing to take away from this thread is that the Coil and Scales, though good and thematic need better stated mechanics and limits. Even only that makes it worth it as it is not it's primary function to provide usefull feedback? Mission acomplished.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T13:52:21-08:00","id":420612,"title":"","content":"Yeah, clarification would be useful. For example, that power where you graft the parts of other supernaturals to yourself, is that supposed to be replacement parts or is it not limited? I mean are there dragons who hunted down a cthonic elder deity to rip off its tentacles so he can be a vampiric doc ock?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T18:15:52-08:00","id":420943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=420079#post420079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Show me the place in Hunter Core that says anything about Entitlements being their own category of merit,</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Endowments, unlike the powers of supernatural beings, are not their own category of Trait. <b>They are simply a new category of Merit</b>, and are purchased with Merit dots just like any other (see \u201cMerits\u201d on p. 67 for the specifics of how each Endowment Merit works). </div> </div> </div> Pg 150, second paragraph, Hunter - The Vigil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4074-sreden","name":"Sreden","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T19:08:38-08:00","id":420981,"title":"","content":"Streden wins the RAW battle. *hands him a crown*<br /> <br /> On his second ever post, too! Welcome to the forums!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T20:47:44-08:00","id":421160,"title":"","content":"There was no Supernatural category of merits when Hunter was written. Technically, nothing in Hunter exists within Vampire by default. IF you allow endowments in a vampire game then you have to decide for yourself if you want to allow a player with access to this coil to gain or regain endowments. There is no &quot;winning&quot; the debate. For all anyone knows, the &quot;endowment category&quot; is the precursor to the supernatural category that came with a new (sort of) edition. Assuming the category remains in the official 2 Ed, it is perfectly reasonable to consider endowment merits also supernatural merits until Hunter 2.0 comes along. It is reasonable to say that vampires can't acquire endowments under any circumstances and hunters lose them upon embrace. You can do as you wish, but there is no basis to say which way is right. As usual, it is a decision for each table.<br /> <br /> That was a nice quote from Hunter, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T15:56:59-08:00","id":1005142,"title":"","content":"Thread Necro!<br /> <br /> Even if you can't take other splat base powers like True Magic, Shapeshifting, etc, Flesh Graft it's still a Diablerists dream come true.<br /> Torpid elder? Figure out what Clan he is and graft several of his parts onto yourself because he likely has decent proficiency in his clan Disciplines. THEN Diablerise him, or not.<br /> Beat some mook into torpor in any fight at all? Graft, graft, graft.<br /> <br /> As cool as it sounds, It is extremely broken IMO.<br /> <br /> Also, for Psychokenesis: Life force. Since Vitae is concentrated life force, cram more of the life into your blood to quasi raise your BP, burn it out of others, lock it into someone to make them un-nourishing, or make it the &quot;flavor&quot; of yourself to establish Vinculum.<br /> <br /> Another fun force is Gravity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 11-18-2016, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T21:03:08-08:00","id":1005222,"title":"","content":"I don't think &quot;life force&quot; is valid or an acceptable substitute for vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T04:58:41-08:00","id":1005306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=1005142#post1005142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even if you can't take other splat base powers like True Magic, Shapeshifting, etc, Flesh Graft it's still a Diablerists dream come true.<br /> Torpid elder? Figure out what Clan he is and graft several of his parts onto yourself because he likely has decent proficiency in his clan Disciplines. THEN Diablerise him, or not.<br /> Beat some mook into torpor in any fight at all? Graft, graft, graft.<br /> <br /> As cool as it sounds, It is extremely broken IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love it how OP it can be, its all the fun gonzo stuff from Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Lure of the flames? It came back in the form of a coil! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T08:16:55-08:00","id":1005356,"title":"","content":"One of the devs said that they won't let the Coil control banes, iirc. Don't have citation for that handy, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T18:25:24-08:00","id":1005532,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't think this Coil would actually see much use at the table. If memory serves, the coil still requires the expenditure of a willpower dot, and vampires don't regain willpower from the day rest. I'm not sure how often people get willpower back at other tables, but I've gone four sessions without ever getting any willpower back, so that might just be my table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T06:38:37-08:00","id":1005688,"title":"","content":"It sounds like your crew doesn't play up Touchstones or work in Mask/Dirge much during normal play. WP shouldn't be much/any harder to come by than Blood if you give it the same amount of time and effort. Of course, there are only so many hours in a night...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T10:39:32-08:00","id":1005755,"title":"","content":"Yeah, we only recently starting playing up touchstones; and Mask/Dirge has trouble coming up at times, but that's been the most reliable way to get willpower back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T01:56:59-08:00","id":1006068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=1005688#post1005688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like your crew doesn't play up Touchstones or work in Mask/Dirge much during normal play. WP shouldn't be much/any harder to come by than Blood if you give it the same amount of time and effort. Of course, there are only so many hours in a night...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But allmost nobody does that. Without blood you die. Without WP... you don't get an opportunity to roll a few more dices? The importance of keeping yourself fed with keeping yourself happy (WP hgh) is just not equal. If for example having high/low WP somehow factored into frenzy rolls - oh boy, would people start stocking up on WP. The question would then come down to whenever its just never spending it, or regaining more of it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T02:20:03-08:00","id":1006074,"title":"","content":"Well, you don't die without blood, you just torpor. A vampire won't starve to death, they'll just be unable to spend the vitae to awaken each night. Not a big difference, except if they died you wouldn't be able to accidentally cut yourself on something, spill your blood and wake up a very hungry vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T13:24:18-08:00","id":1006363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/406978-quick-coil-of-zirnitra-question?p=1006074#post1006074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you don't die without blood, you just torpor. A vampire won't starve to death, they'll just be unable to spend the vitae to awaken each night. Not a big difference, except if they died you wouldn't be able to accidentally cut yourself on something, spill your blood and wake up a very hungry vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only a vampire with BP higher by two than a torpid vampire can wake it up, so no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T17:33:15-08:00","id":1006475,"title":"","content":"WP does factor into frenzy checks. It lets you delay the onset and give a bonus and it allows ride the wave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}